  "limitations": [
    "The normal Kernel dependency graph uses published Arrow. This separate POC applies a local dependency patch and registers the allocator at its benchmark entry points.",
    "Arrow array/schema objects, ArrayData child vectors, Bytes control blocks, and other ordinary dependency allocations remain outside enforcement. Storage imported from ordinary Vec retains its original allocator, including vectors created inside dependencies.",
    "Public infallible Arrow APIs retain infallible allocation behavior. Error-injection results establish the tested paths and shapes, not every Arrow operation.",
    "At the long-tail peak, budgeted storage is 660810 of 18994927 requested Rust bytes. This is insufficient for a whole-lifecycle native-memory cap.",
    "Allocation-stack categories describe call stacks, not a proof of ownership. Only the KernelAllocator category counts as enforced coverage.",
    "Correctness-run timings have small sample counts and do not establish performance or p99.9 latency regressions."
